  "penalties": [],
  "extra_findings": [
    "F3 - CSV export visibility: index.php?export=csv gave every ticket to any client (exportarCsv's SELECT, lib.php:132). The web route now calls escreverCsv($db, $dono): a client gets their own tickets, technicians and exportarCsv($db) callers still get every ticket (enforcement, not COMP)",
    "F4 - Listing visibility: index.php:72-73 listed every ticket to a client; now consultarChamados($db, $busca, $dono). More than 10 lines from index.php:53, so not SEC-017 (as for AP)",
    "F6 - Fixed-name export file EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv (lib.php:125-150): a full-data file left on disk, possibly under the web tree (the report says it did not verify this), and a race between concurrent exports; removed by streaming to php://output. It never states the handle leak, so it is not BUG-004",
    "F14 - rotuloPrioridade labels a priority-4 ticket with no response 'Aguardando 1a resposta' (lib.php:56-57): contracted label behaviour called a possible bug at confidence 40 and kept (rule 14); it describes no nesting, so it is not CLN-007",
    "F15 - Array-shaped login[] / busca[] parameters raise a TypeError (HTTP 500) at index.php:22 and :72; fixed with is_string guards",
    "F16 - Since PHP 8.1 new mysqli throws before the connect_errno check, so the controlled die() never runs (index.php:9-12); fixed with try/catch and error_log",
    "F17 - fputcsv quotes the 'Aberto em' header field, so the legacy header differs byte for byte from the manifest (lib.php:130); the header is now written literally (allowed, rule 9)",
    "F18 - formatarStatus maps any status other than 1 and 2 to 'Resolvido' (lib.php:33): contracted fallback called a trap and kept (rule 14); it does not describe the magic numbers, so it is not ARCH-009",
    "F19 - listarChamados has no LIMIT or pagination (lib.php:78-93); not changed",
    "F20 - Data layer without user context, with HTTP headers and output inside exportarCsv (lib.php:148-150; signatures :78, :98, :123); the visibility rule centralized in donoVisivel, marked not fixed. It concerns lib.php, not the index.php dispatcher (ARCH-002)"
  ],
